IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa5-director-definitions.l4: Companies Act 2006, Part 10, "Meaning of 'director' and 'shadow director'" and "Other definitions": ss 250 to 257 (lines 3293-3368 of
-- ukpga-2006-46.txt). These are the answers every other part takes as inputs, under the names the plan fixes: `s 250 the person occupies the position of director`,
-- `s 251 the person is a shadow director`, `s 252 the person is connected with the director` (plan section 4.2), and the answers to ss 253 to 257 that they use.
--
-- SOURCE: a plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; not the official text.
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER: see coa5-loans-exceptions.l4 (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE and NOTHING as the rule of 2026-10-29 reads them).
-- Subsidiary and holding company are the keel's (s 1159, an input); the rules for interests in shares are Schedule 1 (coa28, an input: the nominal value or the share of voting power the
-- caller has worked out under Schedule 1); treasury shares (s 724, coa15) are disregarded by the caller before the figures are passed in (s 254(5), s 255(5)).

§ `Meaning of "director" and "shadow director" (ss 250 and 251)`

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 250 "Director"
-- ======================================================================================================================

-- "includes any person occupying the position of director, by whatever name called": a list that includes, so a person who does not occupy the position is NOTHING here
-- (an appointed director is a director by the ordinary meaning of the word, which this section does not restate).
-- src:3295 | In the Companies Acts “director” includes any person occupying the position of director, by whatever name called.
@ref s 250 "director" (src:3295-3295)
GIVEN `the person holds a post in the company that carries the position of director, by whatever name it is called` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 250 the person occupies the position of director` MEANS
    IF `the person holds a post in the company that carries the position of director, by whatever name it is called`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "In the Companies Acts “director” includes any person occupying the position of director, by whatever name called"

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 251 "Shadow director"
-- ======================================================================================================================

-- src:3297 | (1) In the Companies Acts “shadow director”, in relation to a company, means a person in accordance with whose directions or instructions the directors of the company are accustomed to act.
@ref s 251(1) "shadow director" (src:3297-3297)
GIVEN `the directors of the company are accustomed to act in accordance with the person's directions or instructions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 251(1) the directors act in accordance with the person's directions or instructions` MEANS
    IF `the directors of the company are accustomed to act in accordance with the person's directions or instructions`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“shadow director”, in relation to a company, means a person in accordance with whose directions or instructions the directors of the company are accustomed to act"

DECLARE `s 251(2) the only reason the directors act` IS ONE OF
    `s 251(2)(a) advice given by that person in a professional capacity`
    `s 251(2)(b) instructions, a direction, guidance or advice given by that person in the exercise of a function conferred by or under an enactment`
    `s 251(2)(c) guidance or advice given by that person in that person's capacity as a Minister of the Crown (within the meaning of the Ministers of the Crown Act 1975)`
    `s 251(2) some other reason`

-- src:3298 | (2) A person is not to be regarded as a shadow director by reason only that the directors act —
-- src:3299 | (a) on advice given by that person in a professional capacity;
-- src:3300 | (b) in accordance with instructions, a direction, guidance or advice given by that person in the exercise of a function conferred by or under an enactment;
-- src:3301 | (c) in accordance with guidance or advice given by that person in that person's capacity as a Minister of the Crown (within the meaning of the Ministers of the Crown Act 1975)
@ref s 251(2) advice, functions and Ministers (src:3298-3301)
GIVEN reason IS A `s 251(2) the only reason the directors act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 251(2) the person is not to be regarded as a shadow director by reason only of that` MEANS
    CONSIDER reason
    WHEN `s 251(2) some other reason` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person is not to be regarded as a shadow director by reason only that the directors act— (a) on advice ..., (b) ... (c) ..."
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 251(3) the purpose` IS ONE OF
    `s 251(3)(a) Chapter 2 (general duties of directors)`
    `s 251(3)(b) Chapter 4 (transactions requiring members' approval)`
    `s 251(3)(c) Chapter 6 (contract with sole member who is also a director)`
    `s 251(3) some other purpose`

-- src:3302 | (3) A body corporate is not to be regarded as a shadow director of any of its subsidiary companies for the purposes of—
-- src:3303 | Chapter 2 (general duties of directors),
-- src:3304 | Chapter 4 (transactions requiring members' approval), or
-- src:3305 | Chapter 6 (contract with sole member who is also a director),
-- src:3306 | by reason only that the directors of the subsidiary are accustomed to act in accordance with its directions or instructions.
@ref s 251(3) a body corporate and its subsidiaries (src:3302-3306)
GIVEN `the person is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1159(1) the company is a subsidiary of the body corporate` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      purpose IS A `s 251(3) the purpose`
      `the only reason is that the directors of the subsidiary are accustomed to act in accordance with its directions or instructions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 251(3) the body corporate is not to be regarded as a shadow director of the subsidiary company for the purpose` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person is a body corporate`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A body corporate is not to be regarded as a shadow director of any of its subsidiary companies"
        IF purpose EQUALS `s 251(3) some other purpose`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for the purposes of— Chapter 2 ..., Chapter 4 ..., or Chapter 6 ..."
        IF NOT `the only reason is that the directors of the subsidiary are accustomed to act in accordance with its directions or instructions`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reason only that the directors of the subsidiary are accustomed to act in accordance with its directions or instructions"
        IF `s 1159(1) the company is a subsidiary of the body corporate` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is a subsidiary of the body corporate is s 1159's answer

-- The answer the other parts take: a shadow director is a person in accordance with whose directions or instructions the directors are accustomed to act, unless (2) or (3) excludes them.
-- src:3296 | 251 “Shadow director”
-- src:3297 | (1) In the Companies Acts “shadow director”, in relation to a company, means a person in accordance with whose directions or instructions the directors of the company are accustomed to act.
-- src:3298 | (2) A person is not to be regarded as a shadow director by reason only that the directors act —
-- src:3299 | (a) on advice given by that person in a professional capacity;
-- src:3300 | (b) in accordance with instructions, a direction, guidance or advice given by that person in the exercise of a function conferred by or under an enactment;
-- src:3301 | (c) in accordance with guidance or advice given by that person in that person's capacity as a Minister of the Crown (within the meaning of the Ministers of the Crown Act 1975)
-- src:3302 | (3) A body corporate is not to be regarded as a shadow director of any of its subsidiary companies for the purposes of—
-- src:3303 | Chapter 2 (general duties of directors),
-- src:3304 | Chapter 4 (transactions requiring members' approval), or
-- src:3305 | Chapter 6 (contract with sole member who is also a director),
-- src:3306 | by reason only that the directors of the subsidiary are accustomed to act in accordance with its directions or instructions.
@ref s 251 "shadow director" (src:3296-3306)
GIVEN `s 251(1) the directors act in accordance with the person's directions or instructions` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 251(2) the person is not to be regarded as a shadow director by reason only of that` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 251(3) the body corporate is not to be regarded as a shadow director of the subsidiary company for the purpose` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 251 the person is a shadow director` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 251(1) the directors act in accordance with the person's directions or instructions` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“shadow director” ... means a person in accordance with whose directions or instructions the directors of the company are accustomed to act"
        IF `s 251(2) the person is not to be regarded as a shadow director by reason only of that` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 251(3) the body corporate is not to be regarded as a shadow director of the subsidiary company for the purpose` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is not to be regarded as a shadow director by reason only that the directors act— ..." and "A body corporate is not to be regarded as a shadow director of any of its subsidiary companies ... by reason only that"
        IF `s 251(1) the directors act in accordance with the person's directions or instructions` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether the directors act in accordance with the person's directions is not known

§ `Other definitions (ss 252 to 257)`

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 253 Members of a director's family
-- ======================================================================================================================

DECLARE `s 253(2) relationship` IS ONE OF
    `s 253(2)(a) the director's spouse or civil partner`
    `s 253(2)(b) any other person (whether of a different sex or the same sex) with whom the director lives as partner in an enduring family relationship`
    `s 253(2)(c) the director's children or step-children`
    `s 253(2)(d) a child or step-child of a person within paragraph (b), who is not a child or step-child of the director`
    `s 253(2)(e) the director's parents`
    `s 253(2) some other relationship`

-- (3): the paragraph (b) partner is excluded if the person is the director's grandparent or grandchild, sister, brother, aunt or uncle, or nephew or niece.
-- src:3333 | (3) Subsection (2)(b) does not apply if the other person is the director's grandparent or grandchild, sister, brother, aunt or uncle, or nephew or niece.
@ref s 253(3) relatives excluded from paragraph (b) (src:3333-3333)
GIVEN `the other person is the director's grandparent or grandchild, sister, brother, aunt or uncle, or nephew or niece` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 253(3) subsection (2)(b) applies to the person` MEANS
    IF `the other person is the director's grandparent or grandchild, sister, brother, aunt or uncle, or nephew or niece`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (2)(b) does not apply if the other person is the director's grandparent or grandchild, sister, brother, aunt or uncle, or nephew or niece"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "does not apply if the other person is" (the subsection says nothing of any other person)

-- src:3327 | (2) For the purposes of this Part the members of a director's family are—
-- src:3328 | (a) the director's spouse or civil partner;
-- src:3329 | (b) any other person (whether of a different sex or the same sex) with whom the director lives as partner in an enduring family relationship;
-- src:3330 | (c) the director's children or step-children;
-- src:3331 | (d) any children or step-children of a person within paragraph (b) (and who are not children or step-children of the director) who live with the director and have not attained the age of 18;
-- src:3332 | (e) the director's parents.
@ref s 253(2) members of a director's family (src:3327-3332)
GIVEN relationship IS A `s 253(2) relationship`
      `s 253(3) subsection (2)(b) applies to the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the child or step-child lives with the director and has not attained the age of 18` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 253(2) the person is a member of the director's family` MEANS
    CONSIDER relationship
    WHEN `s 253(2)(a) the director's spouse or civil partner` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 253(2)(c) the director's children or step-children` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 253(2)(e) the director's parents` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 253(2)(b) any other person (whether of a different sex or the same sex) with whom the director lives as partner in an enduring family relationship` THEN
         IF `s 253(3) subsection (2)(b) applies to the person` EQUALS JUST FALSE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (2)(b) does not apply if the other person is the director's grandparent or grandchild, sister, brother, aunt or uncle, or nephew or niece"
         ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 253(2)(d) a child or step-child of a person within paragraph (b), who is not a child or step-child of the director` THEN
         IF `the child or step-child lives with the director and has not attained the age of 18`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(d) any children or step-children of a person within paragraph (b) (and who are not children or step-children of the director) who live with the director and have not attained the age of 18"
    WHEN `s 253(2) some other relationship` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "the members of a director's family are— (a) ... (e) ..." (no "only")

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 254 Director "connected with" a body corporate
-- ======================================================================================================================

-- (2): "if, but only if, he and the persons connected with him together (a) are interested in shares comprised in the equity share capital of that body corporate of a nominal value equal
-- to at least 20% of that share capital, or (b) are entitled to exercise or control the exercise of more than 20% of the voting power at any general meeting of that body". The interest in
-- shares is counted under Schedule 1 (an input: the nominal value the caller has worked out) and treasury shares are disregarded (subsection (5)) before the figures are passed in.
-- A body corporate with no equity share capital (nominal value nought) has no shares comprised in it, so limb (a) cannot be met: without the "GREATER THAN 0" test the arithmetic "0 is at least 20% of 0" would answer JUST TRUE for it (finding 6 in NOTES.md).
-- src:3336 | (2) A director is connected with a body corporate if, but only if, he and the persons connected with him together—
-- src:3337 | (a) are interested in shares comprised in the equity share capital of that body corporate of a nominal value equal to at least 20% of that share capital, or
-- src:3338 | (b) are entitled to exercise or control the exercise of more than 20% of the voting power at any general meeting of that body.
@ref s 254(2) connected with a body corporate (src:3336-3338)
GIVEN `the nominal value of the shares comprised in the equity share capital of the body corporate in which he and the persons connected with him together are interested` IS A NUMBER
      `the nominal value of the equity share capital of the body corporate` IS A NUMBER
      `the share of the voting power at any general meeting of the body that he and the persons connected with him together are entitled to exercise or control` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 254(2) the director is connected with the body corporate` MEANS
    IF    (`the nominal value of the equity share capital of the body corporate` GREATER THAN 0 AND `the nominal value of the shares comprised in the equity share capital of the body corporate in which he and the persons connected with him together are interested` AT LEAST (`the nominal value of the equity share capital of the body corporate` TIMES 20%))
       OR `the share of the voting power at any general meeting of the body that he and the persons connected with him together are entitled to exercise or control` GREATER THAN 20%
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A director is connected with a body corporate if, but only if, he and the persons connected with him together— (a) are interested in shares ... of a nominal value equal to at least 20% of that share capital, or (b) are entitled to exercise or control the exercise of more than 20% of the voting power"

-- src:3339 | (3) The rules set out in Schedule 1 (references to interest in shares or debentures) apply for the purposes of this section.
@ref s 254(3) Schedule 1 (src:3339-3339)
GIVEN `the interest is one to which a rule in Schedule 1 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 254(3) the rules in Schedule 1 apply for the purposes of this section` MEANS
    IF `the interest is one to which a rule in Schedule 1 applies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Schedule 1 (references to interest in shares or debentures) is coa28's

-- src:3340 | (4) References in this section to voting power the exercise of which is controlled by a director include voting power whose exercise is controlled by a body corporate controlled by him.
@ref s 254(4) voting power controlled through a body corporate (src:3340-3340)
GIVEN `s 255(2) the body corporate that controls the voting power is controlled by the director` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 254(4) voting power controlled by a body corporate controlled by the director counts as controlled by the director` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 255(2) the body corporate that controls the voting power is controlled by the director`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "References in this section to voting power the exercise of which is controlled by a director include voting power whose exercise is controlled by a body corporate controlled by him"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the director controls the body corporate is s 255's answer

-- src:3341 | (5) Shares in a company held as treasury shares, and any voting rights attached to such shares, are disregarded for the purposes of this section.
@ref s 254(5) treasury shares (src:3341-3341)
GIVEN `the shares are held as treasury shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 254(5) the shares and their voting rights are disregarded` MEANS
    IF `the shares are held as treasury shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Shares in a company held as treasury shares, and any voting rights attached to such shares, are disregarded"

-- src:3342 | (6) For the avoidance of circularity in the application of section 252 (meaning of “connected person”) —
-- src:3343 | (a) a body corporate with which a director is connected is not treated for the purposes of this section as connected with him unless it is also connected with him by virtue of subsection (2)(c) or (d) of that section (connection as trustee or partner); and
@ref s 254(6)(a) a connected body corporate (src:3342-3343)
GIVEN `the body corporate is one with which the director is connected under section 254` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is also connected with him by virtue of section 252(2)(c) or (d) (connection as trustee or partner)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 254(6)(a) the body corporate is not treated as connected with the director for the purposes of this section` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the body corporate is one with which the director is connected under section 254`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a body corporate with which a director is connected"
        IF `it is also connected with him by virtue of section 252(2)(c) or (d) (connection as trustee or partner)`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not treated for the purposes of this section as connected with him unless it is also connected with him by virtue of subsection (2)(c) or (d) of that section" (the "unless" is met)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:3344 | (b) a trustee of a trust the beneficiaries of which include (or may include) a body corporate with which a director is connected is not treated for the purposes of this section as connected with a director by reason only of that fact.
@ref s 254(6)(b) a trustee of a trust for a connected body corporate (src:3344-3344)
GIVEN `the beneficiaries of the trust include (or may include) a body corporate with which the director is connected` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that fact is the only reason the trustee would be treated as connected with the director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 254(6)(b) the trustee is not treated as connected with the director` MEANS
    IF `the beneficiaries of the trust include (or may include) a body corporate with which the director is connected` AND `that fact is the only reason the trustee would be treated as connected with the director`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a trustee of a trust the beneficiaries of which include (or may include) a body corporate with which a director is connected is not treated for the purposes of this section as connected with a director by reason only of that fact"

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 255 Director "controlling" a body corporate
-- ======================================================================================================================

-- (2): "if, but only if (a) he or any person connected with him (i) is interested in any part of the equity share capital of that body, or (ii) is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of
-- any part of the voting power at any general meeting of that body, and (b) he, the persons connected with him and the other directors of that company, together (i) are interested in more than
-- 50% of that share capital, or (ii) are entitled to exercise or control more than 50% of that voting power".
-- src:3347 | (2) A director of a company is taken to control a body corporate if, but only if—
-- src:3348 | (a) he or any person connected with him—
-- src:3349 | (i) is interested in any part of the equity share capital of that body, or
-- src:3350 | (ii) is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of any part of the voting power at any general meeting of that body, and
-- src:3351 | (b) he, the persons connected with him and the other directors of that company, together—
-- src:3352 | (i) are interested in more than 50% of that share capital, or
-- src:3353 | (ii) are entitled to exercise or control the exercise of more than 50% of that voting power.
@ref s 255(2) control (src:3347-3353)
GIVEN `he or a person connected with him is interested in any part of the equity share capital of the body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he or a person connected with him is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of any part of the voting power at any general meeting of the body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the share of the equity share capital in which he, the persons connected with him and the other directors of the company together are interested` IS A NUMBER
      `the share of the voting power that he, the persons connected with him and the other directors of the company together are entitled to exercise or control` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 255(2) the director controls the body corporate` MEANS
    IF    (`he or a person connected with him is interested in any part of the equity share capital of the body` OR `he or a person connected with him is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of any part of the voting power at any general meeting of the body`)
       AND (`the share of the equity share capital in which he, the persons connected with him and the other directors of the company together are interested` GREATER THAN 50% OR `the share of the voting power that he, the persons connected with him and the other directors of the company together are entitled to exercise or control` GREATER THAN 50%)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A director of a company is taken to control a body corporate if, but only if— (a) he or any person connected with him— (i) is interested in any part of the equity share capital of that body, or (ii) is entitled to exercise ... any part of the voting power ..., and (b) he, the persons connected with him and the other directors of that company, together— (i) are interested in more than 50% of that share capital, or (ii) are entitled to exercise or control more than 50% of that voting power"

-- src:3354 | (3) The rules set out in Schedule 1 (references to interest in shares or debentures) apply for the purposes of this section.
@ref s 255(3) Schedule 1 (src:3354-3354)
GIVEN `the interest is one to which a rule in Schedule 1 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 255(3) the rules in Schedule 1 apply for the purposes of this section` MEANS
    IF `the interest is one to which a rule in Schedule 1 applies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Schedule 1 (references to interest in shares or debentures) is coa28's

-- src:3355 | (4) References in this section to voting power the exercise of which is controlled by a director include voting power whose exercise is controlled by a body corporate controlled by him.
@ref s 255(4) voting power controlled through a body corporate (src:3355-3355)
GIVEN `s 255(2) the body corporate that controls the voting power is controlled by the director` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 255(4) voting power controlled by a body corporate controlled by the director counts as controlled by the director` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 255(2) the body corporate that controls the voting power is controlled by the director`
