-- s 252 Persons connected with a director
-- ======================================================================================================================

-- (a): members of the director's family (s 253's answer, passed in).
-- src:3311 | (a) members of the director's family (see section 253);
@ref s 252(2)(a) members of the director's family (src:3311-3311)
GIVEN `s 253(2) the person is a member of the director's family` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 252(2)(a) the person is connected with the director as a member of his family` MEANS `s 253(2) the person is a member of the director's family`

-- (b): a body corporate with which the director is connected (as defined in s 254).
-- src:3312 | (b) a body corporate with which the director is connected (as defined in section 254);
@ref s 252(2)(b) a body corporate (src:3312-3312)
GIVEN `s 254(2) the director is connected with the body corporate` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 252(2)(b) the person is connected with the director as a body corporate with which he is connected` MEANS `s 254(2) the director is connected with the body corporate`

-- src:3313 | (c) a person acting in his capacity as trustee of a trust—
-- src:3314 | (i) the beneficiaries of which include the director or a person who by virtue of paragraph (a) or (b) is connected with him, or
-- src:3315 | (ii) the terms of which confer a power on the trustees that may be exercised for the benefit of the director or any such person,
-- src:3316 | other than a trust for the purposes of an employees' share scheme or a pension scheme;
@ref s 252(2)(c) a trustee (src:3313-3316)
GIVEN `the person acts in his capacity as trustee of a trust` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the beneficiaries of the trust include the director or a person who by virtue of paragraph (a) or (b) is connected with him` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the terms of the trust confer a power on the trustees that may be exercised for the benefit of the director or any such person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trust is for the purposes of an employees' share scheme or a pension scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 252(2)(c) the person is connected with the director as a trustee` MEANS
    IF `the person acts in his capacity as trustee of a trust`
       AND (`the beneficiaries of the trust include the director or a person who by virtue of paragraph (a) or (b) is connected with him` OR `the terms of the trust confer a power on the trustees that may be exercised for the benefit of the director or any such person`)
       AND (NOT `the trust is for the purposes of an employees' share scheme or a pension scheme`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The following persons (and only those persons) are connected with a director of a company— ... (c) a person acting in his capacity as trustee of a trust— (i) the beneficiaries of which include the director or a person who by virtue of paragraph (a) or (b) is connected with him, or (ii) the terms of which confer a power on the trustees that may be exercised for the benefit of the director or any such person, other than a trust for the purposes of an employees' share scheme or a pension scheme"

-- src:3317 | (d) a person acting in his capacity as partner—
-- src:3318 | (i) of the director, or
-- src:3319 | (ii) of a person who, by virtue of paragraph (a), (b) or (c), is connected with that director;
@ref s 252(2)(d) a partner (src:3317-3319)
GIVEN `the person acts in his capacity as partner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a partner of the director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a partner of a person who by virtue of paragraph (a), (b) or (c) is connected with the director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 252(2)(d) the person is connected with the director as a partner` MEANS
    IF `the person acts in his capacity as partner` AND (`the person is a partner of the director` OR `the person is a partner of a person who by virtue of paragraph (a), (b) or (c) is connected with the director`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The following persons (and only those persons) are connected with a director of a company— ... (d) a person acting in his capacity as partner— (i) of the director, or (ii) of a person who, by virtue of paragraph (a), (b) or (c), is connected with that director"

-- src:3320 | (e) a firm that is a legal person under the law by which it is governed and in which—
-- src:3321 | (i) the director is a partner,
-- src:3322 | (ii) a partner is a person who, by virtue of paragraph (a), (b) or (c) is connected with the director, or
-- src:3323 | (iii) a partner is a firm in which the director is a partner or in which there is a partner who, by virtue of paragraph (a), (b) or (c), is connected with the director.
@ref s 252(2)(e) a firm (src:3320-3323)
GIVEN `the person is a firm that is a legal person under the law by which it is governed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director is a partner in the firm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a partner in the firm is a person who by virtue of paragraph (a), (b) or (c) is connected with the director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a partner in the firm is a firm in which the director is a partner or in which there is a partner who by virtue of paragraph (a), (b) or (c) is connected with the director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 252(2)(e) the person is connected with the director as a firm` MEANS
    IF `the person is a firm that is a legal person under the law by which it is governed`
       AND (   `the director is a partner in the firm`
            OR `a partner in the firm is a person who by virtue of paragraph (a), (b) or (c) is connected with the director`
            OR `a partner in the firm is a firm in which the director is a partner or in which there is a partner who by virtue of paragraph (a), (b) or (c) is connected with the director`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The following persons (and only those persons) are connected with a director of a company— ... (e) a firm that is a legal person under the law by which it is governed and in which— (i) the director is a partner, (ii) a partner is a person who, by virtue of paragraph (a), (b) or (c) is connected with the director, or (iii) a partner is a firm in which the director is a partner or in which there is a partner who, by virtue of paragraph (a), (b) or (c), is connected with the director"

-- (3): "References in this Part to a person connected with a director of a company do not include a person who is himself a director of the company."
-- src:3324 | (3) References in this Part to a person connected with a director of a company do not include a person who is himself a director of the company.
@ref s 252(3) a person who is himself a director (src:3324-3324)
GIVEN `the person is himself a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 252(3) a person connected with a director includes the person` MEANS
    IF `the person is himself a director of the company`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "References in this Part to a person connected with a director of a company do not include a person who is himself a director of the company"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person who is himself a director of the company"

-- The answer the other parts take. "(and only those persons)": the persons in (a) to (e) and no others, except a person who is himself a director ((3), and in s 239 not (3): s 239(5)(d)).
-- src:3308 | 252 Persons connected with a director
-- src:3309 | (1) This section defines what is meant by references in this Part to a person being “connected” with a director of a company (or a director being “connected” with a person).
-- src:3310 | (2) The following persons (and only those persons) are connected with a director of a company—
-- src:3311 | (a) members of the director's family (see section 253);
-- src:3312 | (b) a body corporate with which the director is connected (as defined in section 254);
-- src:3313 | (c) a person acting in his capacity as trustee of a trust—
-- src:3314 | (i) the beneficiaries of which include the director or a person who by virtue of paragraph (a) or (b) is connected with him, or
-- src:3315 | (ii) the terms of which confer a power on the trustees that may be exercised for the benefit of the director or any such person,
-- src:3316 | other than a trust for the purposes of an employees' share scheme or a pension scheme;
-- src:3317 | (d) a person acting in his capacity as partner—
-- src:3318 | (i) of the director, or
-- src:3319 | (ii) of a person who, by virtue of paragraph (a), (b) or (c), is connected with that director;
-- src:3320 | (e) a firm that is a legal person under the law by which it is governed and in which—
-- src:3321 | (i) the director is a partner,
-- src:3322 | (ii) a partner is a person who, by virtue of paragraph (a), (b) or (c) is connected with the director, or
-- src:3323 | (iii) a partner is a firm in which the director is a partner or in which there is a partner who, by virtue of paragraph (a), (b) or (c), is connected with the director.
@ref s 252 persons connected with a director (src:3308-3323)
GIVEN `s 252(3) a person connected with a director includes the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 252(2)(a) the person is connected with the director as a member of his family` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 252(2)(b) the person is connected with the director as a body corporate with which he is connected` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 252(2)(c) the person is connected with the director as a trustee` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 252(2)(d) the person is connected with the director as a partner` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 252(2)(e) the person is connected with the director as a firm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 252 the person is connected with the director` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 252(3) a person connected with a director includes the person` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "References in this Part to a person connected with a director of a company do not include a person who is himself a director of the company"
        IF    `s 252(2)(a) the person is connected with the director as a member of his family` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           OR `s 252(2)(b) the person is connected with the director as a body corporate with which he is connected` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           OR `s 252(2)(c) the person is connected with the director as a trustee` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           OR `s 252(2)(d) the person is connected with the director as a partner` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           OR `s 252(2)(e) the person is connected with the director as a firm` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF    `s 252(2)(a) the person is connected with the director as a member of his family` EQUALS JUST FALSE
           AND `s 252(2)(b) the person is connected with the director as a body corporate with which he is connected` EQUALS JUST FALSE
           AND `s 252(2)(c) the person is connected with the director as a trustee` EQUALS JUST FALSE
           AND `s 252(2)(d) the person is connected with the director as a partner` EQUALS JUST FALSE
           AND `s 252(2)(e) the person is connected with the director as a firm` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The following persons (and only those persons) are connected with a director of a company"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a limb is answered NOTHING (the family list of s 253 is not closed, or s 254's figures are not known)

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 256 Associated bodies corporate
-- ======================================================================================================================

-- src:3362 | (a) bodies corporate are associated if one is a subsidiary of the other or both are subsidiaries of the same body corporate, and
@ref s 256(a) associated bodies corporate (src:3362-3362)
GIVEN `s 1159(1) one body corporate is a subsidiary of the other` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1159(1) both bodies corporate are subsidiaries of the same body corporate` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 256(a) the bodies corporate are associated` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 1159(1) one body corporate is a subsidiary of the other` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 1159(1) both bodies corporate are subsidiaries of the same body corporate` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 1159(1) one body corporate is a subsidiary of the other` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `s 1159(1) both bodies corporate are subsidiaries of the same body corporate` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "bodies corporate are associated if one is a subsidiary of the other or both are subsidiaries of the same body corporate"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether one is a subsidiary of the other is s 1159's answer and is not known

-- src:3363 | (b) companies are associated if one is a subsidiary of the other or both are subsidiaries of the same body corporate.
@ref s 256(b) associated companies (src:3363-3363)
GIVEN `s 1159(1) one company is a subsidiary of the other` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1159(1) both companies are subsidiaries of the same body corporate` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 256(b) the companies are associated` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 1159(1) one company is a subsidiary of the other` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 1159(1) both companies are subsidiaries of the same body corporate` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 1159(1) one company is a subsidiary of the other` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `s 1159(1) both companies are subsidiaries of the same body corporate` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "companies are associated if one is a subsidiary of the other or both are subsidiaries of the same body corporate"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether one is a subsidiary of the other is s 1159's answer and is not known

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 257 References to company's constitution
-- ======================================================================================================================

DECLARE `s 257(1) matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 257(1)(a) a resolution or other decision come to in accordance with the constitution`
    `s 257(1)(b) a decision by the members, or a class of members, that is treated by virtue of any enactment or rule of law as equivalent to a decision by the company`
    `s 257(1) some other matter`

-- src:3365 | (1) References in this Part to a company's constitution include—
-- src:3366 | (a) any resolution or other decision come to in accordance with the constitution, and
-- src:3367 | (b) any decision by the members of the company, or a class of members, that is treated by virtue of any enactment or rule of law as equivalent to a decision by the company.
-- src:3368 | (2) This is in addition to the matters mentioned in section 17 (general provision as to matters contained in company's constitution).
@ref s 257 references to the company's constitution (src:3365-3368)
GIVEN matter IS A `s 257(1) matter`
      `s 17 the matter is one mentioned in section 17` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 257 the matter is part of the company's constitution for the purposes of this Part` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `s 257(1)(a) a resolution or other decision come to in accordance with the constitution` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 257(1)(b) a decision by the members, or a class of members, that is treated by virtue of any enactment or rule of law as equivalent to a decision by the company` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 257(1) some other matter` THEN
         CONSIDER `s 17 the matter is one mentioned in section 17`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE -- (2): "This is in addition to the matters mentioned in section 17"
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "References in this Part to a company's constitution include— (a) ... (b) ..."
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the matter is one mentioned in s 17 is s 17's answer
